# RELEASE-LEDGER.jsonl — the durable record of every exact-public proof verdict (XPUB-06).
#
# One JSON object per line, appended by script/append_release_ledger.sh, which is invoked by the
# `record-ledger` job in .github/workflows/exact-public-proof.yml. Append-only: existing lines are
# never rewritten or reordered, so this file's git history IS the audit trail.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AND NOT A LONGER ARTIFACT RETENTION. crosswake is a public repository, so the
# uploaded-artifact retention ceiling sits far below the horizon over which a release verdict must
# stay readable; no retention value satisfies the criterion. Git has no expiry, so the copy of record
# is committed here. The `exact-public-proof` artifact keeps its existing retention untouched — it is
# a fast-path signal, not the copy of record.
#
# OUTCOMES ARE RECORDED FAITHFULLY, INCLUDING NON-SUCCESS. `outcome` is the literal job result:
# success, failure, cancelled or skipped. A pass-only ledger could not distinguish "the proof failed"
# from "the proof never ran", which is precisely the equivalence milestone v23.0 exists to break.
#
# BACKFILL BOUNDARY: backfill_boundary_run_id=31325689640
# Every entry whose run_id is LESS THAN OR EQUAL TO 31325689640 was backfilled by hand on
# 2026-09-17 from GitHub Actions run records; GitHub run ids increase monotonically, so the
# comparison is decidable for every line. Every entry with a run_id GREATER THAN that boundary was
# written live by the proof workflow at release time. Source and per-row provenance of the backfill,
# each read with `gh run view <run_id> --json jobs` against szTheory/crosswake:
#
#   run 28675522926 (2026-07-03, crosswake 0.2.0, "Publish to Hex.pm" = success)
#     outcome `skipped`: this run predates the exact-public proof entirely — NO post-publish proof
#     job of any kind ran in it. That is exactly the "the proof never ran" state, and recording it
#     as skipped rather than omitting the release is the point of the field.
#   run 28691886814 (2026-07-04, crosswake_chimeway 0.1.0, publish = success)
#     outcome `failure`: job "Clean-room proof — crosswake_chimeway resolvability + doctor" = failure.
#   run 31325689640 (2026-08-09, crosswake_sigra 0.1.3, publish = success)
#     outcome `failure`: job "Clean-room proof — crosswake_sigra resolvability + doctor" = failure.
#
# For the three backfilled rows the outcome is the conclusion of that run's post-publish proof lane
# for that coordinate — the clean-room proof job, which is what the exact-public proof was extracted
# out of in Phase 173. No backfilled row claims an exact-public proof job that did not exist.
#
# There is deliberately no `success` row among the backfilled entries: this repository's post-publish
# proof lane has not recorded a passing verdict for any of the releases above. That absence is the
# history, not a limitation of the writer — script/append_release_ledger.sh writes a success line
# identically, as test/crosswake/release_candidate/release_ledger_test.exs demonstrates.
